        "original_id": "a19ab27a-7aab-50d2-917e-e7b22ff1caee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Civil Defence Forces, Revolutionary United Front, National Patriotic Front of Liberia\n- People: Foday Sankoh, Charles Taylor, Joseph Momoh\n- Events: Sierra Leone Civil War\n- Groups: Kamajors, Mende ethnic group\n\nFacts:\n- The Sierra Leone Civil War began on 23 March 1991 when the Revolutionary United Front, supported by special forces from Charles Taylor’s National Patriotic Front of Liberia, intervened in Sierra Leone to try to overthrow the Joseph Momoh government.\n- Foday Saybana Sankoh, born on 17 October 1937, founded and led the Revolutionary United Front during the Sierra Leone Civil War.\n- The Civil Defence Forces was a paramilitary organization that fought in the Sierra Leone Civil War from 1991 to 2002.\n- Much of the Civil Defence Forces was made up of the Kamajors, a group that is part of the larger Mende ethnic group.\n- The Sierra Leone Civil War lasted 11 years from 1991 to 2002, affected the whole country, and caused more than 50,000 deaths.\n- Foday Saybana Sankoh died on 29 July 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
